{
  "analysis": "The system is actually x86_64 but running under OrbStack with Rosetta translation (explaining why QEMU 5.2.0 fails with a Rosetta syscall error). QEMU 8.2.2 from apt runs but the VM is stuck at EIP=0x5f1 with identical registers across samples, indicating an infinite loop in BIOS code. The screen shows only a cursor in 720x400 text mode. Since the image is compatible with QEMU 5.2.0, the issue is likely BIOS/firmware compatibility. We should try using the SeaBIOS firmware from the QEMU 5.2.0 build with QEMU 8.2.2.",
  "plan": "Kill the current QEMU, then try launching QEMU 8.2.2 using the QEMU 5.2.0 pc-bios directory (which contains the compatible SeaBIOS). Also try different combinations like `-L /tmp/qemu-5.2.0/pc-bios`, `-cpu 486`, and Cirrus VGA. Take screenshots and check CPU registers to see if the VM progresses.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "kill $(cat /tmp/qemu.pid 2>/dev/null) 2>/dev/null || true; sleep 1; rm -f /tmp/qemu-monitor.sock /tmp/qemu.pid\nls -la /tmp/qemu-5.2.0/pc-bios/bios.bin /tmp/qemu-5.2.0/pc-bios/vgabios.bin /tmp/qemu-5.2.0/build/pc-bios/bios.bin 2>/dev/null || true\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "qemu-system-i386 \\\n  -L /tmp/qemu-5.2.0/pc-bios \\\n  -hda /app/isos/win311.img \\\n  -snapshot \\\n  -m 128 \\\n  -boot c \\\n  -vnc 0.0.0.0:1 \\\n  -chardev socket,id=mon0,path=/tmp/qemu-monitor.sock,server=on,wait=off \\\n  -mon chardev=mon0,mode=readline \\\n  -daemonize \\\n  -pidfile /tmp/qemu.pid\necho \"Exit: $?\"\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sleep 15\n",
      "duration": 15.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "vncsnapshot -allowblank localhost:1 /tmp/vnc-test2.jpg 2>&1 || true\npython3 -c \"from PIL import Image; img=Image.open('/tmp/vnc-test2.jpg'); print('Size:', img.size); colors=img.getcolors(maxcolors=100000); print('Colors:', len(colors) if colors else '>100000'); print('Top:', sorted(colors, key=lambda x:-x[0])[:15] if colors else 'N/A')\"\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 << 'EOF'\nimport socket, time\ns = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)\ns.connect(\"/tmp/qemu-monitor.sock\")\ntime.sleep(0.3)\ns.recv(4096)\ns.send(b\"info registers\\n\")\ntime.sleep(0.5)\nr1 = s.recv(4096).decode()\nprint(r1)\ntime.sleep(2)\ns.send(b\"info registers\\n\")\ntime.sleep(0.5)\nr2 = s.recv(4096).decode()\nprint(r2)\nprint(\"CPU advancing:\", r1 != r2)\ns.close()\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    }
  ]
}
